{"id": "mm6316a4", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011CggGVaSBfNUVTMrms1FNs", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 9699, "output": 3613}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "```json\n{\"id\": \"mm6316a4\",\n \"data_focus\": {\"v\": \"yes\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"vaccination will prevent an estimated 322 million illnesses, 21 million hospitalizations, and 732,000 deaths\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Coverage for many childhood vaccine series was near or above 90% for much of the period.\"}]},\n \"outcome_types\": [\n  {\"v\": \"count/rate\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Among 78.6 million children born during 1994– 2013, routine childhood immunization was estimated to prevent 322 million illnesses\"}]},\n  {\"v\": \"binary/categorical\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"coverage also was higher in the VFC era, as measured by NIS, than in the pre-VFC era\"}]},\n  {\"v\": \"continuous\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Vaccination will potentially avert $402 billion in direct costs and $1.5 trillion in societal costs\"}]}\n ],\n \"analytic_depth\": [\n  {\"v\": \"summary\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Coverage for many childhood vaccine series was near or above 90% for much of the period.\"}]},\n  {\"v\": \"comparison\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"coverage also was higher in the VFC era, as measured by NIS, than in the pre-VFC era\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Since 1996, coverage with 1 dose of a measles-containing vaccine has exceeded Healthy People § targets of 90%\"}]}\n ],\n \"study_design\": [\n  {\"v\": \"cost/economic\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"employed methods previously used for children born in 2009\"}]},\n  {\"v\": \"evaluation or monitoring\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"To summarize the impact of the U.S. immunization program on the health of all children\"}]},\n  {\"v\": \"before/after or trend\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"coverage also was higher in the VFC era, as measured by NIS, than in the pre-VFC era\"}]}\n ],\n \"methods_quotes\": [\n  {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"USIS and NHIS data were from parental recollection of vaccines received, and NIS data were obtained through provider report.\"},\n  {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"A decision analysis birth cohort model was constructed using data on immunization coverage\"},\n  {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Costs were adjusted to 2013 dollars, and future costs related to disease were discounted at 3% annually.\"},\n  {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The cost analysis was conducted from both health-care (direct) and societal (direct and indirect) perspectives, and net present value (net savings) was calculated.\"}\n ],\n \"confidence\": \"high\",\n \"uncertain_fields\": []}\n```", "type": "text"}]}